#!/usr/bin/python3 -I
"""
mp35n - a tiny master-password keyring for Chrome's cookie encryption.

Chrome (Linux) gets a per-app secret from the desktop portal and derives its
cookie key from it. mp35n implements the portal's Secret backend, so the key
is written straight into Chrome's pipe and never crosses D-Bus. The legacy
org.freedesktop.secrets interface remains only to refuse sessions; it never
returns the secret.

Chrome only *encrypts* with the portal key (cookie prefix v12) when the
SecretPortalKeyProviderUseForEncryption feature is on; without it Chrome
fetches the key, ignores it, and writes v10 cookies under the public
"peanuts" key. `mp35n run` always passes that feature.

The key is only written when the process holding the pipe's read end is
exactly the Chrome process `mp35n run` just launched and authorized with
the one-time token from the unlock, and that process is the root-owned
Chrome binary with an allowed command line and a clean environment.

Run `35 help` for commands. Install/uninstall is handled by ./install.sh in this folder.
"""

